      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This issue is caused by the latest client update of VRChat and not related to Meta Quest firmware.\n****************************************************\nMore importantly, this problem occurs not only in Quest2, but also in Quest1.\n*****************************************************\nI checked it with [build-1156] on 2021-12-08-14:00 (PST), and at that time the photos were still saved and could be picked up from the device.\nHowever, a minute later, as soon as I updated to [build-1159], the photo saving feature stopped working.\nIn both situations, Quest was v35 firmware.\nTherefore, build-1159 of VRChat contains a bug, metaphorically, which turned Quest users' VR cameras into cam recorders that forgot to insert the SD-memory-card.\nI would very much appreciate it if you could find out the cause and resolve the issue.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
